        <p>TWO LIBERAL VICTORIES. Mr. Morley has been returned for the Montrose Burghs by a majority of 1.993 over the Unionist candidate, the polling being 4,565 to 2,572. At the general election last year the Liberal majority was only 1,132. The poll- ing at Southamptom on Saturday to fill the Parliamen- tary vacancy caused by the unseating on petition of Mr, Chambarlayne (Conservative) resulted in Sir F. }l, Evans, the Liberal candidate, being returned by 5.557 votes, as against 5,522 votes cast for Mr. G. Candy, Q.C., the Conservative candidate. Mr. C. A. Gibson, the Socia- list candidate, only polled 271 votes.</p>
